  "description": "Do Woo-Jin, a bassist in an indie band, was an oddball with a strangely gloomy aura—and an almost absurd amount of bad luck. After his previous bands disbanded one after another, leaving him with nowhere to go, a third chance finally came his way. It was in this new band that he met Choi Hui-Su…\n\nFor Hui-Su, who had lived an ordinary life—his biggest act of rebellion being the pentagram tattoo on his forearm—Woo-Jin, whose thoughts were impossible to read, felt nothing but awkward. During a post-practice drinking session, while the band members chatted boisterously, Woo-Jin answered half-heartedly with an uncomfortable expression—until his gaze landed on Hui-Su’s tattoo.\n\n*“…A pentagram symbolizes the devil.”*\n\nFor the first time, a spark of interest flickered in Woo-Jin’s otherwise empty eyes. But wait, what had their bandmate said while introducing Woo-Jin earlier?\n\n*\"I warned you, didn’t I? That guy’s a total nutcase.\"*\n\n(Source: Bomtoon, translated)",
